					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "LUT 3D IN\n\nThe LUT 3D In node is an input node that allows users of the patch to import their own LUT's. Because this is an Input node, it will show up in both the Wire dashboard and the Arena\/Avenue interface.\n\nThe node panel can be used to load a default LUT file (.cube).\nThis can be used for testing purposes or to ship if as the default file.\nTo add a file, hit the cogwheel icon next to the value and select \"Browse\".\n\nThe node panel can also be used to set an \"Options Count\" allowing you to create multiple preset resources for the user to select from.\n\nLUT is shorthand for Look-Up Table.\nThis is a .CUBE file containing mathematical instructions to replace colors. \nThis process is done pixel by pixel with a very high accuracy.\nLUT's can be seen as color grading presets\n"
					}
				},
